{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he stood between the dead, etc.</b> He seized the angel and held him against his will. The angel said to him: Let me do my mission! He said to him: Moses commanded me to stop you. The angel said to him: I am the emissary of the Omnipresent and you are the emissary of Moses. He said to him: Moses says nothing of his own accord but from the mouth of the Mighty One. If you do not believe — behold, the Holy One, blessed be He, and Moses are at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting; come with me and ask. And this is what is said: <b>And Aaron returned to Moses.</b> Another interpretation: Why through the incense? Because Israel were murmuring and complaining about the incense, saying: It is a deadly poison — through it Nadav and Avihu died, through it two hundred and fifty men were burned. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: You shall see that it is a plague-stopper, and it is the sin that kills (Mekhilta Exodus 17)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:24.376150439Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}